  "content": {
    "title": "Luka Doncic injury update: Lakers star injures left hamstring in loss vs Thunder",
    "text": "April 2, 2026Updated April 3, 2026, 1:31 a.m. CTLuka Doncic exited the Los Angeles Lakers' 139-96 loss to the OKC Thunder with a left hamstring injury Thursday night at Paycom Center.The Lakers ruled Doncic out for the remainder of the game near the start of the fourth quarter. Doncic appeared to tweak his hamstring mid play before walking toward the baseline and laying down. The injury occurred with 7:39 remaining in the third quarter as the Lakers trailed OKC 90-58.Doncic previously had been grabbing at his hamstring before Los Angeles went into the halftime break trailing by 31.Lakers coach JJ Redick said that LA's medical staff cleared Doncic to play after having his hamstring checked at halftime.\"We wish for the best,\" Lakers guard Austin Reaves said. \"Obviously you don't want to see anybody get hurt, but you just hold on to some faith for the best news possible. I've gotten to know him last year and a half. He's a competitor, so he'll do all he can do to put himself in a position to come back when he can.\"Doncic will undergo an MRI on Friday to determine the extent of his left hamstring injury, according to ESPN's Dave McMenamin.He exited the game with 12 points, seven assists, four rebounds and six turnovers on 3-of-10 shooting from the field.Doncic needs just one more game played to meet the NBA's 65-game requirement for to be considered for major postseason awards. He was named the Western Conference Player of the Month for March on Thursday after averaging 37.5 points, 8.0 rebounds, and 7.4 assists.Los Angeles (50-27) has just five games remaining in the regular season with a road matchup against the Dallas Mavericks up next on Sunday night. The Lakers' next home game will be a rematch against OKC on Tuesday.Doncic's loss comes at a crucial time for the Lakers as the team is in pursuit of locking up the third seed in the Western Conference playoff picture. LA currently holds a one game lead in the third seed over Denver in the standings with Houston trailing by 2.5 games and Minnesota behind by 3.5 games.And with Doncic's status up in the air with the playoffs set to kick off in two weeks away, the Lakers are aiming to stay optimistic.\"We're already out with Marcus (Smart) right now and now Luka,\" Lakers star LeBron James said. \"Obviously we'll be tested without the head of the snake — don't want to make no conclusions — but we'll see what happens from there.\" Luka Doncic statsEntering play Thursday:Games played: 63Points per game: 33.8Assists per game: 8.3Rebounds per game: 7.8Field-goal shooting: 47.7%3-point shooting: 36.8%Free-throw shooting: 77.9%Jordan Davis covers high school sports for The Oklahoman. Have a story idea for Jordan? He can be reached atjdavis@oklahoman.com or on X/Twitter at@thejordancdavis. Sign up forThe Varsity Club newsletter to access more high school coverage. Support Jordan’s work and that of other Oklahoman journalists by purchasing adigital subscription today at subscribe.oklahoman.com.",
